{"case_id":"T5033","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API entry point","state mutation","input semantics"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":94,"affected_functions":["ares_dns_rr_set_ttl","LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput"],"reason":"S1 adds the public mutating API `ares_dns_rr_set_ttl`, but H0 only obtains TTL values through `ares_dns_rr_get_ttl` and serializes unmodified records with `ares_dns_write`. It never invokes the new setter, controls its `ttl` argument, tests its `dns_rr == NULL` protocol, or exercises serialization after setter-driven state mutation. Because this API did not exist in S0, the uncovered surface is introduced by the commit.","evidence":["`include/ares_dns_record.h` newly declares `ares_dns_rr_set_ttl(ares_dns_rr_t *dns_rr, unsigned int ttl)`.","`src/lib/record/ares_dns_record.c` newly implements a NULL-input branch returning `ARES_EFORMERR` and a non-NULL branch assigning `dns_rr->ttl = ttl`.","H0's `test/ares-test-fuzz.c` calls `ares_dns_rr_get_ttl(rr)` while printing parsed records, but contains no call to `ares_dns_rr_set_ttl`.","H0 calls `ares_dns_write(dnsrec, ...)` only after parsing and inspection, without fuzz-controlled setter mutation."],"recommended_action":"Extend `LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput` to select parsed resource records, derive TTL values from fuzz input, call `ares_dns_rr_set_ttl`, verify the resulting value through `ares_dns_rr_get_ttl`, and pass the mutated record to `ares_dns_write`; also exercise the NULL-record error path."}
